      "class": "V-C",
      "explanation": "HOL4 specifies only `RESULT (Result t) = t`. The transparent `RESULT_pkg` also makes `RESULT (Clash t) = t` provable by `rfl`. For example, HOL4’s saved equation permits a selector that returns 0 on `Clash 1`, while Lean proves that this input returns 1.",
      "repair": "private opaque RESULT_pkg {α : Type u} : {f : result α → α // ∀ t, f (Result t) = t} :=\n  ⟨fun r => match r with | Result t => t | Clash t => t, fun _ => rfl⟩",
      "confidence": 1,
      "lean_check": "import CandleLean.HolSyntaxLib\n\nexample : Candle.RESULT (Candle.result.Clash (1 : Nat)) = 1 := rfl",
      "hol4_check": "∃f : num result -> num. (∀t. f (Result t) = t) ∧ f (Clash 1) = 0"
    }
  ]
